{{Quote|Most Haruun Kal kids didn't get plucked and sent to mystical academies. If they grew up at all, they grew up hard. And leaving was a matter of will and sacrifice.|Azita Cruuz|<ref name="Mace Windu 2">[[Mace Windu 2|''Mace Windu'' 2]]</ref>}}
'''Haruun Kal''' was a [[planet]] within the [[Haruun Kal system]], a [[star system]] in the [[Dustig sector]] of the [[Mid Rim Territories]], and the [[homeworld]] of [[Jedi Master]] [[Mace Windu]].

==Description==
{{Quote|I took in the sunrises off the southern gas marshes and fished in the shores of Lake Haruuni, which is so high in the mountains the fish practically float out of the water.|Azita Cruuz|<ref name="Mace Windu 3" />}}
[[File:LakeHaruuni-MaceWindu3.png|thumb|left|250px|Azita Cruuz at Lake Haruuni]]
A [[planet]],<ref name="Force Users">{{EncyclopediaCite|Mace Windu and Other Users of the Force}}</ref> Haruun Kal was located in the [[Haruun Kal system]] in the [[Dustig sector]] of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]], in grid square M-17 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="Appendix" /> Its [[capital]] [[city]] was [[Pelek Baw]]. The planet had southern gas [[Swamp|marshes]], and [[Lake Haruuni]] was high enough in the [[mountain]]s that its [[fish]] practically floated out of the [[water]].<ref name="Mace Windu 3" />

==History==
{{Quote|Listen, I'm not sure who I'm going to sell the formula to. The Jedi, the Trade Federation, the Hutts, the Pyke Syndicate. But I'm warming to the idea of it being someone from our homeworld Haruun Kal.|Azita Cruuz, to Mace Windu|<ref name="Mace Windu 2" />}}
[[File:PelekBaw-MaceWindu3.png|250px|right|thumb|Pelek Baw]]
Legends stated that Haruun Kal was originally settled by marooned [[Jedi]], a single crashed [[Starship|ship]] bringing new life that spread across the planet.<ref name="The Glass Abyss" />

Every Haruun toddler was given an inoculation that left a distinctive scar, appearing as a raised, circular bump on the upper chest, which was utilized by natives as a method of recognizing one another offworld. Children typically had a hard upbringing, and the planet had a notable [[death]] rate among its youth. Leaving the planet was a matter of will and sacrifice. [[Mace Windu]] was a child taken from<ref name="Mace Windu 2" /> his [[homeworld]]<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> to become a [[Jedi Master]] and champion of the [[Jedi Order]].<ref name="Mace Windu">{{Databank|mace-windu|Mace Windu}}</ref> Scores of children and parents lived in [[Pelek Baw]], where parents either doted on their offspring or ignored them. [[Azita Cruuz]] was orphaned when her parents died during the crossing, and upon arriving she was treated cruelly by other children.<ref name="Mace Windu 3" />

[[File:BillabaVsGrievous-Kanan11.png|left|thumb|250px|Grievous and Billaba fought on Haruun Kal]]
During the [[Clone Wars]], the planet was the site of a [[Battle of Haruun Kal|battle]] between the [[Galactic Republic]] and [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], in which [[Supreme Martial Commander of the Separatist Droid Armies|Confederate Supreme Commander]] [[General]] [[Grievous]] led his [[Separatist Droid Army|droid forces]] against Republic forces led by [[Jedi General]] [[Depa Billaba]]. Billaba personally fought Grievous,<ref name="The Canyons of Kardoa" /> resulting in her defeat and the loss of ninety percent of her [[Soldier|troops]].<ref name="The Corridors of Coruscant">[[Kanan 7|''Kanan'' 7]]</ref>

As a result of a conflict left over from the Clone Wars, the [[Imperial Military]] was deployed to counter an [[Bombardment of Haruun Kal|insurrection on Haruun Kal]]. The battle ended with an [[orbital bombardment]] under the [[Base Gamma One]] protocol, ending the insurrection with an [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] victory. The bombardment was hot enough to boil the seas and send Imperials still on the ground into convulsions.<ref name="Final Order" /> Although the forests were reduced to ash, new [[Lammas]] tree saplings were beginning to sprout<ref name="Ultimate Cookbook">''[[Star Wars: The Ultimate Cookbook]]''</ref> by [[34 ABY]].<ref name="TUC date">{{UltimateCookbookDate}}</ref>

{{Planet-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|&hellip;''This'' particular Jedi&mdash;''Master Depa Billaba''&mdash;is hardly a threat. Our intelligence identifies her as a ''failed'' commander, a ''liability'' to the Republic. In fact, according to this, you ''yourself'' faced her on ''Haruun Kal''&hellip;where you ''decimated'' her troops and very nearly ''ended'' her life.|[[General]] [[Kleeve]], to General [[Grievous]]|<ref name="The Canyons of Kardoa">[[Kanan 9|''Kanan'' 9]]</ref>}}
Haruun Kal was first mentioned in the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in a featurette<ref name="Liberty on Ryloth featurette">[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars The Complete Season One|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' The Complete Season One]]&mdash;Featurette: "Liberty on Ryloth"</ref> included in [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars The Complete Season One|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' The Complete Season One]], a box set available on [[Wikipedia:Blu-ray|Blu-ray]] or [[Wikipedia:DVD|DVD]] that included the entire [[The Clone Wars: Season One|first season]] of the canon animated series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''<ref name="The Complete Season One">[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars The Complete Season One|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' The Complete Season One]]</ref> that was released on [[November 3]], [[2009]].<ref name="Star Wars: The Clone Wars The Complete Season One release date">{{Amazon|url=Star-Wars-The-Clone-Season/dp/B002L3RVCY|text=Star Wars: The Clone Wars: Season 1}}</ref> It was originally created for "[[Children of the Force (comic story)|Children of the Force]]," a [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] story included in ''[[Star Wars Tales 13]]''.<ref name="Children of the Force">{{Tales|13|Children of the Force (comic story)}}</ref> In [[Mace Windu 4|''Mace Windu'' 4]], [[the Shroud]] incorrectly refers to Haruun Kal as an Outer Rim world.<ref name="Mace Windu 4">[[Mace Windu 4|''Mace Windu'' 4]]</ref>

